{"title":"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle is inscribed in a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. Tangents to the circle parallel to the sides of the triangle are contructed. Each of these tangents cuts off a triangle from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. In each of these triangles, a circle is inscribed. Find the sum of the areas of all four inscribed circles (in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the tangent to the in circle parallel to BC cut AB,AC at D &amp; E respectively. Similarly let the tangent to the same parallel to AB cut AC,BC at F &amp; G respectively and the tangent to the same parallel to AC cuts BC,AB at H,M respectively. Let the incircle touch the sides BC,CA,AB at P,Q,R respectively and let the points of contact of MH,FG,DE with the in circle be X,Y,Z respectively. Then perimeter of BHM = BH+HX+XM+MB=BH+HP+MR+BM=BP+BQ=2(s-b) and similar results follow!\n</p>\n<pre>Each of the triangles BHM,CGF,ADE are similar to ABC. \n</pre>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f0ccef4165412c6cafe5279e6fee3b11adf33d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BHM]/[BCA] = \\text{(perimeter of BHM/perimeter of BCA)}^2 ={(2s-2b)/(a+b+c)}^2 ={(c+a-b)/(c+a+b)}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"842\" height=\"22\" />\n</p>\n<pre>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/674c44e65cd1c693b60d79a861e22b99020aafa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BHM]+[CGF]+[ADE]=[ABC]/(a+b+c)^2 { ( b+c-a)^2 + (c+a-b)^2 + (a+b-c)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"706\" height=\"20\" />\n</pre>\n<p><br />\nDenote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d33cc80fa8f093e155c5be46d2e5d9da3d7e1ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/5155aa866a797f98b826ed02392324eb8d7c0b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ABC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1adeb1c0eb2b60a7118ea6c85159efd986aec0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[BHM]}{[ABC]} = \\left(\\frac{(BHM)}{(ABC)}\\right)^{2} =\\left(\\frac{c+a-b}{c+a+b}\\right)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"325\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67ad64a3b6d83abe6c0b223f743644abeec6e431.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BHM]=\\left(\\frac{c+a-b}{c+a+b}\\right)^{2}\\cdot [ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"256\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>We know, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec390fe1cb2c516af134a92ceb187c0a5568e1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the radius of the incircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b911bf24a12c83ef538accf36adffabd8dcf1c23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BHM$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/a/00aa98e4ab6e4bdcdeb39d8f59b32df4e832ae0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{1}= 2 \\cdot \\frac{[BHM]}{(BHM)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"129\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Area of the incircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b911bf24a12c83ef538accf36adffabd8dcf1c23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BHM$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad16ac626290a07b90bd2b95fe7b8401f3eef95a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\pi \\cdot 4 \\cdot (\\frac{[BHM]}{(BHM)})^{2}= 4\\pi \\frac{(c+a-b)^{2}}{(c+a+b)^{4}} \\cdot ([ABC])^{2}\\]\" width=\"380\" height=\"44\" />\nArea of the incircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/b/66bd4fa3ea41a412d78fc778c3bbbbd7952c4906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi (\\frac{[ABC]}{a+b+c})^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"114\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Sum of the area of the 4 incircles:\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/19299874547ded3201003f4f67ae604d987d4194.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4 \\pi ([ABC])^{2}\\left[\\frac{(c+a-b)^{2}+(b+c-a)^{2}+(c+a-b)^{2}}{(a+b+c)^{4}}\\right]+4\\pi (\\frac{[ABC]}{a+b+c})^{2}\\]\" width=\"566\" height=\"43\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b66c86ada17b3d9d68220cbd6ff4598f3559bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=4 \\pi \\frac{([ABC])^{2}}{(a+b+c)^{2}}\\left[\\frac{(c+a-b)^{2}+(b+c-a)^{2}+(c+a-b)^{2}+(a+b+c)^{2}}{(a+b+c)^{2}}\\right]\\]\" width=\"587\" height=\"43\" />\n\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd322f52ac69489786946628db0d2a77e8b7c7ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=16 \\pi \\frac{([ABC])^{2}(a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2})}{(a+b+c)^{4}}\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO\" title=\"1964 IMO\">1964 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1964 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017152725\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 145/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4501/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.714      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%   15.714      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8266:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017152725 and revision id 143758. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}